> Out of sheer curiosity, what's the earliest possible corpse that'll
> give me poison resistance? And how much do amulets of proof against
> poison cost, usually?

Eating poisonous corpses will often (not always, see the spoiler posted
later) give you poison resistance.  While you lose some stats for doing
so, if you have some means of regaining the stats immediately,... say, a
unicorn horn or the spell 'restore ability'... it's well worth it to
hang out near the top and gain poison resistance off some dead things
before venturing much further.

Sure, the poison could be deadly off those too.  But since going forward
far enough without poison resistance gives roughly the same chance for
survival in the long run (spiked pits are very, very common)... YMMV.
And unicorns show up fairly early.

